  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI can't believe the synapse matrix server implementation still uses old school single processing instead of multi threading. Especially if you have a server with lots of users, you really need multi threading for performance.\r\n\r\nI know, workers is a nice solution for horizontal scaling, but hey, most servers have multiple cores now and it would IMHO be a real shame not to use these. I'm not a python expert, but it seams to me that this should be a high priority requirement for an application like this, especially if you have lots of users.\r\n\r\nOr did I miss something?\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\n\r\nVictor.\r\n",
